/* book exam traps: Sign slip: y[n] + a1y[n − 1] = x[n] becomes y[n] = −a1y[n − 1] + x[n]. The feedback multiplier is −a1. | For y[n] − 0.5y[n − 1] = x[n] the characteristic equation is λ − 0.5 = 0. Writing 1 − 0.5λ = 0 gives the false root λ = 2 and a false 'unstable'. | Guessing a constant forced response when λ = 1 is a root: the guess vanishes. Multiply it by n. | Order versus input length: N counts output delays and M counts input delays; a second-order equation can have any number of b coefficients. | Calling a simple root on the unit circle stable. It is only marginally stable, and an input at that frequency gives an output that grows without bound. */
